 Below 7500 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9d9ffdde0bb758c8a2dddc264c33b72111a8975a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.9d9ffdde0bb758c8a2dddc264c33b72111a8975a.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Watch","headline":"Flash Flood Watch issued August 19 at 1:40PM MDT until August 19 at 8:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding and debris flows caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinue to be possible over the Aspen Acres burn scar.\n\n* WHERE...Aspen Acres Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 8 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Aspen Acres burn scar is expected\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Aspen\nAcres burn scar should prepare for potential debris flow. Be sure\nto stay up to date with information from local authorities. Heavy\nrainfall could trigger flash flooding of low-lying areas, street\nflooding, and debris flows in and near recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-08-19T20:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Wet Mountains between 6300 and 10000Ft; Wet Mountains above 10000 Ft; Pueblo Vicinity/Pueblo County Below 6300 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.89cf3d25e80748ae24a920d75305dbaccd47d33a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.89cf3d25e80748ae24a920d75305dbaccd47d33a.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-19T18:47:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 191847 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1247 PM MDT Wed Aug 19 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Burn scar flash flooding and marginally severe storms possible this evening. - Daily afternoon showers and storms will continue into early next week, along with slowly warming temperatures. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH THURSDAY/... Issued at 1